4 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "77353fd7-ee88-5664-aec8-e00589b061d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270391 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270391 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270391 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "81cab381-305e-5227-96c9-4247414173f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270468 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270468 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270468 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8abda789-acc5-5411-8952-794fc73da646" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270745 #edb/ref 1080 "II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270745 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270745 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a4e8d21b-4e62-5248-a3d7-8afaad5786f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270786 #edb/ref 1080 "II and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270786 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270786 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aa256175-82e0-56ad-9450-2d16ed6ca6ba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270827 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270827 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270827 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "af2612fc-39ba-5012-92ba-66032676ab46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270949 #edb/ref 1080 "I only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270949 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270949 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "be53ddb2-3789-59ea-8a22-87a097d55924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270005 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186270827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271774 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "94b73dce-7f8c-597e-ae8e-4e20e2b2ff1f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270271 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186269347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271828 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "afe26b88-241f-530c-8ccf-982cdb7e7d4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270391 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186269702 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271926 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ecf48405-f1ff-5682-8eff-4a48eebe4c60" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271926 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142474" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix and \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ 0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}?\n$$\n\nI. $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1$\n\nII. $A$ is invertible\n\nIII. $\\text{rank}(A)<4$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4927fd87-c83e-52d3-b9bb-877110a8c514" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272347 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is a $4\\times 4$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{4} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=4=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, since \n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)=\\{{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\,|\\,{x}_{1},{x}_{2}\\in R\\}\n$$\n\nwe conclude that \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 4,$ or equivalently $\\text{rank}(A)<4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1069 "q-142476" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $\\text{__________}$ .*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $det(A)=0$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}$\n\nIII. $A$ has $8$ pivot columns" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7036dc73-9ca4-59f2-b983-11eaacfb5a4b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272349 #edb/ref 1074 "If $A$ is an $8\\times 8$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=8=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $det(A)=0$* $\\,\\times $  \n\nSince the matrix $A$ is invertible, it must be  $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then  $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{16}.$*  $\\,\\times $\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem,  we have $\\text{Col}(A)={R}^{8}.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n*If $A$ is a $8\\times 8$ matrix and $A$ is invertible,  then $A$ has $8$ pivot columns.* $\\,✓$ \n\nSince $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\text{dim(Col}(A))=8,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $8$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345426 #edb/ref 1080 "I and III only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345426 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186345426 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "097b8a1b-b44d-5e76-97c8-b4c1a59a0e59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346284 #edb/ref 1080 "I and II only" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346284 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186346284 #e